 "documents": {
  "attachments": [
   {
    "name": "crowd_plan.txt",
    "text": "Looking after people on the day: Eastfield Heritage Run Half Marathon, Saturday 24 April 2027\n\nGrace Lindqvist, Race Director, Eastfield Athletics\n\nWe expect about 650 people altogether, including 650 runners. Few people come just to watch.\n\nWhere people will watch\nWe've set out three viewing spots with barriers: at the finish by Harbour Green, at the turn by Salter Way, and at the start by the top of Bell Street. We measured them, and at about two people to the square metre they take around 850 between them, which is more than we expect to come.\n\nHow we start the race\nWe set off in 3 waves, four minutes apart, with runners sorted by the time they expect to run. That thins everyone out before the first corner. The pens close five minutes before each wave goes.\n\nWho's helping\nWe've got 13 stewards in tabards, about one for every 50 people, with 2 supervisors in charge of sections. Each has a set position on a rota, and all come to a briefing an hour before the start.\n\nGetting everyone away\nRunners walk through a one-way funnel after the line, out to the recovery area, and leave by the north gate. Spectators have two marked ways out, and a steward stands at each to keep it clear. We reckon the whole place empties in 25 minutes.\n\nWho's in charge\nGrace Lindqvist runs the event from the control point with a radio to every supervisor. They can hold a wave, stop the race, or make an announcement over the speakers to move people along. Supervisors call it in if a pen or viewing spot looks to be getting too full.\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "insurance.txt",
    "text": "Meridian Mutual Insurance\nCertificate of Insurance\n\nWe certify that a policy of event public liability insurance has been issued as follows.\n\nPolicy: GL-221719\nInsured: Eastfield Athletics\nEvent covered: Eastfield Heritage Run Half Marathon\nLocation of event: Marina Point\nCover starts: 2027-01-01\nCover ends: 2027-12-31\nLimit of indemnity: $5,000,000 any one event\n\nSigned on behalf of the insurer, 2027-01-23\nCertificate reference EV-91512\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "medical_plan.txt",
    "text": "Eastfield Heritage Run Half Marathon - medical notes\nSaturday 24 April 2027 / gun 08:00 / 650 runners / half marathon\ncontact Grace Lindqvist 555-0188\nNo ambulance will be stationed at the race; any ambulance would come through the 911 system.\n\nFIRST AID\n3 posts (start, finish, midpoint). 10 qualified first aiders. nowhere more than 1.5km from a post. 2 bike responders w/ defibs\n\nWEATHER / WATER\nwater every 2.5k. forecast check -48h and -2h. >28C earlier start or shorter course. >32C cancel. foil + warm tent at finish if cold/wet\n\nHOSPITAL\nValley Regional Hospital, 11km from finish. pickup point the top of Bell Street, route walked w/ first aiders. ED told date + numbers\n\nCOMMS\nradios on medical channel at all posts + bikes, phones backup. amb calls go via medical lead, who gives crew the barrier to come to\n\nLEAD\nFatima Haddad, registered paramedic, on site from -1hr til last runner in. can withdraw any runner\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "race_plan.txt",
    "text": "Eastfield Heritage Run Half Marathon - race notes\nEastfield Athletics / contact Grace Lindqvist 555-0188\nSaturday 24 April 2027, gun 08:00, course closes 11:30\nhalf marathon (21k), approx 650 entered\n\nROUTE\nBell Street, Salter Way and Orchard Road. all closed. major x-ings: High Street and Ferry Road. finish Harbour Green\n\nWIDTHS\nstart Bell Street (11m). Salter Way 14m. Orchard Road 10m + wide pavements + verge most of way\n\nOTHER\nnumbers from the top of Bell Street 1hr before. chip timing. water on course. results online same day\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "traffic_plan.txt",
    "text": "Traffic arrangements for the Eastfield Heritage Run Half Marathon, Saturday 24 April 2027\n\nFrom Grace Lindqvist, Race Director, Eastfield Athletics\n\nWe have tried to think through what happens on the roads on race day. The race is a half marathon, it starts at 08:00, and it goes through the Marina Point area. Police attendance has been requested, but we have not had an answer yet.\n\nClosing the roads\nWe need the following closures, and Signal Hill Traffic Services will put out the barriers and signs for us. Bell Street from Linden Avenue to Hatter Street, 06:45 until 12:00. Salter Way from Spring Way to Linden Avenue, 06:45 until 12:00. Orchard Road from Lamb Street to Chapel Row, 06:45 until 12:00.\n\nCrossings\nWhere we cross a major road we will have people stationed from 06:45 until the last runner is through. At High Street, where it meets Salter Way, there will be 3 traffic marshals with stop/go boards and a supervisor. At Ferry Road, where it meets Orchard Road, there will be 2 traffic marshals with stop/go boards and a supervisor.\n\nThe route has changed little from last time. Where it has changed, we have tried to keep a clear run for the field, and we welcome any comments from the Events Office on how signed diversions are usually handled in the city.\n\nGetting around the closures\nWe've worked out the way round for drivers and Signal Hill Traffic Services will sign it. Traffic off Bell Street goes via Victoria Road and Queen's Road, signed from Linden Avenue. Traffic off Salter Way goes via Prince Street and Queen's Road, signed from Spring Way. Traffic off Orchard Road goes via Prince Street and Dock Road, signed from Linden Avenue.\n\nEmergency vehicles\nWe keep one lane clear the whole way, 3.5 metres or more, for ambulances and fire engines. Every barrier has someone with a radio on our channel, and they can have it open within two minutes. Our controller on the day has direct numbers for police and ambulance control.\n\nLetting people know\nEvery house and shop on the closed streets gets a letter three weeks before and a reminder a week before. We'll put up the yellow notice boards ten days ahead, and we've told the bus company the times.\n\nAfterwards\nOnce it's all over the team will collect the cones and barriers, and everyone can get back to normal.\n"
   }
  ],
  "cover_letter": "23 January 2027\n\nEvents Office\nCity of Port Halden\n\nDear Events Officer,\n\nPlease find our application below.\n\nWe are applying for a street race permit for the Eastfield Heritage Run Half Marathon on Saturday 24 April 2027. We expect 650 runners over half marathon, starting at 08:00 in the Marina Point area. The completed form and the attachments (crowd_plan.txt, insurance.txt, medical_plan.txt, race_plan.txt, traffic_plan.txt) are enclosed.\n\nPlease let me know if you need anything else.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nGrace Lindqvist\nRace Director, Eastfield Athletics\ngrace@eastfieldac.example / 555-0188\n",
